{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/stories/04-cross-process-package-alignment.md | sed -n '40,80p'\"","aggregated_output":"    40\t- [tech-design.md](../tech-design.md), [tech-design-server.md](../tech-design-server.md), [tech-design-client.md](../tech-design-client.md)\n    41\t- [test-plan.md](../test-plan.md)\n    42\t\n    43\t### Acceptance Criteria\n    44\t<!-- Jira: Acceptance Criteria field -->\n    45\t**AC-4.1:** A package may contain pinned artifact versions produced by multiple processes in the same project.\n    46\t\n    47\t- **TC-4.1a: Mixed-producer package allowed**\n    48\t  - Given: A process is publishing a package in a project\n    49\t  - When: The package includes versions produced by more than one process in that project\n    50\t  - Then: The package can be published successfully\n    51\t- **TC-4.1b: Cross-project package member blocked**\n    52\t  - Given: A package member version belongs to a different project\n    53\t  - When: The package is published\n    54\t  - Then: The system rejects that package publication\n    55\t\n    56\t**AC-4.2:** A process can publish a package from artifact versions in its current package-building context, defined as current process references plus versions already pinned in that same process's current package draft/edit context, even when those versions were produced by other processes.\n    57\t\n    58\t- **TC-4.2a: Publishing process can package referenced upstream versions**\n    59\t  - Given: A process currently references artifact versions produced by earlier processes in the same project\n    60\t  - When: The process publishes a package\n    61\t  - Then: Those referenced upstream versions may be included in the package\n    62\t- **TC-4.2b: Unrelated project artifact version not in current package-building context is blocked**\n    63\t  - Given: A project contains an artifact version that is neither currently referenced by the publishing process nor already pinned in that process's current package draft/edit context\n    64\t  - When: The process publishes a package\n    65\t  - Then: The system rejects use of that unrelated artifact version\n    66\t- **TC-4.2c: Earlier pinned version remains eligible**\n    67\t  - Given: A process is reopening or editing a package that already pins an earlier artifact version from the same project\n    68\t  - When: The process republishes or re-exports that package context\n    69\t  - Then: That already-pinned earlier version remains eligible even if a newer version now exists\n    70\t\n    71\t**AC-4.3:** Package review resolves pinned member versions rather than drifting to whichever artifact version is current later.\n    72\t\n    73\t- **TC-4.3a: Package member opens pinned version**\n    74\t  - Given: A package member pins a specific artifact version\n    75\t  - When: The user opens that member in package review later\n    76\t  - Then: The pinned version is shown\n    77\t- **TC-4.3b: Newer later artifact version does not replace pinned package member**\n    78\t  - Given: A newer artifact version exists after the package was published\n    79\t  - When: The user reviews the package\n    80\t  - Then: The package still resolves the originally pinned member version\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
