{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design-server.md | sed -n '90,150p'\"","aggregated_output":"    90\t\n    91\t| Module | Status | Responsibility | Dependencies | ACs Covered |\n    92\t|--------|--------|----------------|--------------|-------------|\n    93\t| `app.ts` | MODIFIED | Wire `ReviewContextService` and `PackageContextService` into `DefaultArtifactReviewService`, `DefaultPackageReviewService`, `DefaultReviewWorkspaceService`, and process-surface review enablement; register any new review/package context dependencies at app composition time | Fastify service composition | AC-3 through AC-5 |\n    94\t| `schemas/review.ts` | MODIFIED | Expand route schemas and response-code expectations so target-specific review endpoints can return exact 404 codes for missing explicit versions and unavailable package members | shared contracts | AC-3, AC-4, AC-5 |\n    95\t| `routes/review.ts` | MODIFIED | Map review lookup result kinds and `AppError` subclasses to exact request codes instead of collapsing all null reads into `REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` | review services, route schemas | AC-3 through AC-5 |\n    96\t| `platform-store.ts` | MODIFIED | Provide low-level durable reads and writes for artifacts, versions, current refs, package contexts, and package snapshots; stop owning review-context composition | Convex queries/mutations, shared contracts | AC-1 through AC-5 |\n    97\t| `review-context.service.ts` | NEW | Resolve aligned process review context from current refs, package context, and published package snapshots; answer `availableTargets`, direct-access eligibility, and review enablement | `PlatformStore`, pure helpers | AC-3, AC-5 |\n    98\t| `package-context.service.ts` | NEW | Upsert current package-building context, seed from published snapshot on reopen, and validate publish eligibility against same-project + in-context rules | `PlatformStore`, pure helpers | AC-4 |\n    99\t| `artifact-review.service.ts` | MODIFIED | Resolve artifact review through process review context, not artifact ownership; return zero-version empty state and exact missing-version failures | `PlatformStore`, `review-context.service.ts`, renderer | AC-2, AC-3, AC-5 |\n   100\t| `package-review.service.ts` | MODIFIED | Resolve mixed-producer package members, keep unrelated members readable when one degrades, and classify selected-member failures accurately | `PlatformStore`, `review-context.service.ts`, `artifact-review.service.ts` | AC-4, AC-5 |\n   101\t| `review-workspace.service.ts` | MODIFIED | Bootstrap the review workspace from aligned review context and keep bounded degraded target states inside the workspace envelope | process access, review services | AC-3, AC-5 |\n   102\t| `artifact-section.reader.ts` | MODIFIED | Build project artifact summaries from project identity + latest version projection only | `PlatformStore` | AC-1, AC-2 |\n   103\t| `process-work-surface.service.ts` | MODIFIED | Compute review control enablement from aligned review context instead of same-process production shortcuts | `review-context.service.ts` | AC-3 |\n   104\t| `convex/artifacts.ts` | MODIFIED | Remove artifact-row process ownership and keep checkpoint writes version-oriented | `artifactVersions`, process refs | AC-1, AC-2 |\n   105\t| `convex/processPackageContexts.ts` + members | NEW | Durable current package-building context with ordered pinned version members | Convex schema | AC-4 |\n   106\t| `convex/packageSnapshots.ts` | MODIFIED | Publish immutable snapshots from aligned same-project/current-context rules instead of same-process-producer rules | Convex schema, package context validation | AC-4 |\n   107\t\n   108\t## Durable State Model\n   109\t\n   110\tThe durable model after Epic 5 has five artifact/package layers:\n   111\t\n   112\t1. project artifact identity\n   113\t2. artifact versions with provenance\n   114\t3. per-process current artifact refs\n   115\t4. per-process current package-building context\n   116\t5. immutable published package snapshots\n   117\t\n   118\t### 1. `artifacts`: Project Identity Only\n   119\t\n   120\tCurrent state still stores `processId` on the artifact row. Epic 5 removes it.\n   121\t\n   122\t#### Table Shape\n   123\t\n   124\t```ts\n   125\texport const artifactsTableFields = {\n   126\t  projectId: v.string(),\n   127\t  displayName: v.string(),\n   128\t  createdAt: v.string(),\n   129\t};\n   130\t```\n   131\t\n   132\t#### Why\n   133\t\n   134\tThe artifact row should answer only one question: \"what durable artifact\n   135\tidentity exists in this project?\" If the row also says \"this belongs to process\n   136\tX,\" the rest of the system will keep trying to use that shortcut for review\n   137\teligibility, package publication, and process lineage. Epic 5 removes the\n   138\tshortcut rather than trying to teach every caller not to use it.\n   139\t\n   140\t### 2. `artifactVersions`: Keep Provenance Here\n   141\t\n   142\t`artifactVersions` remains the version-provenance table. Epic 5 does not change\n   143\tits core purpose; it leans harder on it.\n   144\t\n   145\t#### Table Shape\n   146\t\n   147\t```ts\n   148\texport const artifactVersionsTableFields = {\n   149\t  artifactId: v.id('artifacts'),\n   150\t  versionLabel: v.string(),\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
